You must:

-Give 10% of your gold to the co-aligned high priest on the Astral
Plane. (Reference to tithing)
-As soon as possible, wear a T-shirt or Hawaiian shirt. Do not take it
off for the rest of the game. (Reference to garments)
-As soon as possible, carry a blessed potion of oil with you at all
times. You may put it away in a container, however, the !oOil must be
in your possession until the end of the game. (Reference to
consecrated oil.)
-Have a Quest Guardian accompany you throughout the entire quest. He
only has to be on the same level as you at all times, from the time
you start the quest, until you end it.
-Leave a blank spellbook #named "The Book of Mormon" on the last level
of the Quest. (Both of these requirements equate the Quest to a Mormon
mission.)

You cannot:

-Steal directly from shops. You may allow a pet to steal for you.
-Drink a potion of booze.
-Have sex.
-Commit murder.
-Lie to a vault guard about your name.
-Steal money from a vault that has a guard (unguarded vaults are free
game).
-Be an athiest.
-Be a vegetarian.

Optional:
-You must, as soon as possible, #name one of your rings "CTR". Wear
this ring or another ring #named CTR for the rest of the game.
-You must have a tame human or foocubus adjacent to you when you
ascend. He/she must be of a gender opposite of yours.
-You may only step into a co-aligned temple if you are wearing a
shirt. Stepping into a square that causes the priest to speak to you
("Pilgrim!...") is acceptable, but you cannot go any further if you
aren't wearing a shirt.


You may polymorph into a demon, kill any A, change alignment, use an
athame, anger your god, be seduced/charmed by a nymph, genocide, be a
cannibal, and kill your pet, if you wish to do so. A Mormon character
can be any role and any alignment.

All of these are references to Mormonism, of course. You probably
won't get these if you aren't Mormon or don't live in Utah.



